.TH KYTHOS-ASSIST 1 "2027" "KythOS Kernal" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kythos-assist \- inspect shell commands using offline documentation and metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kythos-assist
.RB [ --explain | --complete | --intent | --diagnose ]
.RB [ --status " N" ]
.RB [ --json ]
.RI "command line or description words"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Discover installed executables and inspect local manual declarations, versions
from the package database, and literal shell syntax. No inspected executable,
help option, version probe or proposed command is run. No typed text, history
or environment dump is saved or sent to a service.
.PP
Interactive Bash adds builtin, alias, function and completion names without
reading definitions or calling dynamic completion callbacks. The standalone
executable cannot inspect its parent shell's unexported definitions.
.PP
Quote a whole shell expression so the current shell passes it as data. The
inspector describes pipelines, conditionals, quoting, redirections and literal
paths. It does not evaluate expansions, substitutions, globbing, here-documents
or compound programs. Missing documentation produces explicit uncertainty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --explain
Explain the command and documented options. This is the default mode.
.TP
.B --complete
Print locally grounded candidate names. Nothing is inserted or executed.
.TP
.B --intent
Preview a reviewed phrase or typo correction, or search local descriptions.
Description matches do not establish an argument grammar.
.TP
.B --diagnose
Inspect an explicitly supplied exit status and command context. No earlier
output or shell history is collected. An exit status alone cannot prove cause.
.TP
.B --status N
Supply the failed command's exit status for diagnosis.
.TP
.B --json
Emit a structured local result with title, lines, candidates and proposal.
.SH INTERACTIVE BINDINGS
F1 inspects the current Bash edit buffer. Tab previews a recognized correction;
a second Tab or Right Arrow copies it for review. Ordinary Enter executes.
Native completion, history and custom bindings retain their normal behavior.
.SH PRIVACY
Explanations do not repeat arbitrary argument values. Recognized credential
arguments suppress correction previews. Positional secrets cannot reliably be
identified: use the application's protected input rather than command-line
credentials. Assistance reads neither command history nor arbitrary file
contents, and does not send data to an online model.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
kythos-assist --explain 'ls --all ./docs | grep report > matches'
kythos-assist --complete 'systemctl --no'
kythos-assist --intent 'compress files'
kythos-assist --diagnose --status 127 'missing-tool argument'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kythos-help (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR man (1)
